# Build output
#
# `go build ./cmd/adamic` drops the binary at the repository root, and dedication/build.sh leaves its
# object and binary beside the source. One line per binary, so nothing platform-specific reaches a
# commit by way of `git add -A`.
/adamic
dedication/dedication
dedication/dedication.o

# Never ignore *.a here.
#
# `.a` is Adamic's source extension, and it was Unix's static-library extension first, which is why
# GitHub's C and C++ templates (and many global ignore files) list `*.a`. Stage 0 asks git whether
# each source is ignored and refuses to build one that is (docs/0.1.md), so an `*.a` line anywhere in
# this file would make every Adamic program unbuildable. The runtime never ships as a `.a`.

# The morning report: written overnight for Kirk to read, not part of the history.
.overnight.md

# Local caches
.cache/

# Operating systems and editors, as cohere carries them. Finder writes a .DS_Store into any directory
# it displays; two appeared here, at the root and under internal/, while the repository was only
# being read.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.localized
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/

# Stray logs
#
# Nothing here writes a .log on purpose. Test runs are sent to a log rather than through a pipe (see
# CLAUDE.md), and that file should never reach a commit.
*.log

# Static lint dispatch is regenerated before builds and tests.
/stage1/cohere/lint/.generated/

# Local run output from fixture and gate tools.
/logs/
